# Cloudflare Pages response headers — repository-controlled browser security
# policy for app.waytrace.co (audit finding #18). Vite copies this file from
# public/ into dist/, and Pages applies it to every response.
#
# CSP is scoped to exactly what this SPA loads (verified in audit Session 12):
#   - scripts/styles/fonts: bundled, same-origin ('self'); no inline <script>.
#   - style-src allows 'unsafe-inline' for React/Recharts inline style attrs.
#   - connect-src: same-origin + the Worker API host (all fetch() targets).
#   - Stripe checkout / billing portal / Google OAuth are top-level navigations
#     (window.location), NOT fetch/iframe, so they need no CSP allowance.
#   - img/worker allow data: and blob: for client-generated QR codes.
#
# ROLLOUT: CSP ships Report-Only first (violations log to the browser console
# without blocking) so a full click-through can confirm zero violations; then
# it is promoted to the enforcing Content-Security-Policy header. The other
# headers are non-breaking and enforce immediately.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://link-manager-worker.lee-1dd.workers.dev; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
